# TypeScript rules

- `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`. No `any`, no `as` on external data, no `@ts-ignore`.
- Validate every trust boundary (body, query, params, JWT header/claims, env, parent API, JWKS)
  with `zod`; use only the parsed value.
- SQL is parameterised (`$1, $2`). Never build SQL from input with template strings.
- Modules holding secrets or DB access (`db`, `crypto`, `session`) import `server-only`.
  `src/lib/sso.ts` and `src/lib/config.ts` hold only public keys/URLs and stay importable by
  `src/proxy.ts` and `node:test`.
- Client errors are generic; details go to logs without personal data.
- Prefer the platform: `node:crypto`, `fetch`, route handlers, Proxy.
- Tests: `node:test` + `node:assert/strict`, files in `test/*.test.ts`, run with `npm test`
  (Node 24 strips types natively; import local files with the `.ts` extension).

```ts
// ❌ trusts client input for identity
const userId = req.headers.get('x-user-id');
// ✅ identity only from the verified token
const { sub } = await requireSession();
```
